162
00:07:11.069 --> 00:07:17.009
to be able to compartmentalize the data as needed.

163
00:07:17.009 --> 00:07:18.129
If we go back to our slides

164
00:07:18.129 --> 00:07:20.329
you'll see that how this works

165
00:07:20.329 --> 00:07:23.889
is it reduces complexity and provides a scalable solution

166
00:07:23.889 --> 00:07:25.769
when creating new projects.

167
00:07:25.769 --> 00:07:28.569
RID cell streaming can be enabled

168
00:07:28.569 --> 00:07:31.850
and disabled using the enable streaming option

169
00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:33.329
in the world settings.

170
00:07:34.149 --> 00:07:35.990
The following templates use a world partition

171
00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:39.790
but have enabled streaming disabled by default.

172
00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.629
So you can turn that on if you need to.

173
00:07:41.629 --> 00:07:42.709
So when editing your world

174
00:07:42.709 --> 00:07:44.990
actors can be added anywhere

175
00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:47.470
and are automatically assigned to a grid cell

176
00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:49.910
based on their spatially loaded setting

177
00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.189
found in their detail panels

178
00:07:52.189 --> 00:07:54.310
of the world partition section.

179
00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:57.709
So you can manage all of this as you need

180
00:07:57.709 --> 00:07:59.230
and you can adjust things.

181
00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.029
Now, again, it's worthy.

182
00:08:01.029 --> 00:08:02.949
You have to test this out.

183
00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:07.009
Because you need to decide once you get your layout

184
00:08:07.009 --> 00:08:09.589
once you know exactly what your player is going to be

185
00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:12.649
you can determine how the cells are being digested

186
00:08:12.649 --> 00:08:13.889
where you need to put them

187
00:08:13.889 --> 00:08:15.810
and where the concentration of

188
00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.769
as you working through your scene

189
00:08:17.769 --> 00:08:19.790
where you need to optimize things

190
00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.970
